cycard 1
# The palette. A separate source from the card for the reason samples/06-open-world's palette is a
# separate source from its city: two independent imports into one cook is what makes "a one-asset
# change invalidates only the derivations that depend on it" a thing the outcome column of
# `cy_build build` can be read for. Change a colour here and the card's import stays cached.
#
# `cook:card` concatenates in DECLARATION ORDER, so the palette arrives before the card that names
# its colours, and `card.cpp` therefore never has to resolve a colour it has not seen yet.

colour ground   14  17  24
colour panel    24  29  40
colour ink     232 236 245
colour dim     140 150 170
colour accent   86 168 255
colour warn    240 176  64
colour absent  214  92  92
colour good    104 198 128
